idence":[{"quote":"During this period, the SFC continues to accept applications and submissions via existing channels.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u3.737"},{"quote":"Starting 30 November 2024, ie, after the parallel run period, applications and submissions of investment products administered by IPD must be submitted via e-IP.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"}],"formalization":null,"hypothesis":"Existing channels remain permitted after cutover for cases opened during the parallel run.","substantive_effect":"Later submissions in existing cases would be exempt from e-IP routing."},{"assessment":"The missing independent integration date creates operational uncertainty but does not establish an exception to the express routing requirement.","evidence":[{"quote":"The current submission requests from IPD via the IP E-submission system will be integrated into e-IP, including reporting of net asset values, large redemptions and suspensions of dealing.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"}],"formalization":null,"hypothesis":"Existing IP E-submission reports are exempt until a separately confirmed integration date.","substantive_effect":"Some covered reports could continue through the legacy system after 30 November 2024."},{"assessment":"Unsupported. The heading does not override the operative permissive wording.","evidence":[{"quote":"Full adoption of e-IP","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u7.1505"},{"quote":"In addition, e-IP users can also settle recurring annual fees associated with relevant investment products through the new system.","unit_id":"d19f9ecf9fd26.u8.1528"}],"formalization":null,"hypothesis":"Full adoption makes annual-fee payment through e-IP mandatory.","substantive_effect":"Standalone fee payments through other channels would fail a mandatory payment-channel control."}],"move":"exception-attachment","parent_node_id":"node.ba6f46eafccfb5756de6aa69","proposal_status":"One supported reading retained; potential exceptions remain unresolved rather than formalized without